+      "oracle": "real",
+      "expect": "survived",
+      "why": "Two writes to distinct attributes of the same in-memory dataclass with no read of each other's field between them (reason reads only report.unpushed, set earlier on both orders); squash() is single-threaded and the Report is observed only after it returns, so the order is inert on every path the suite can reach. It would stop being inert only if something observed the half-written Report mid-assignment, which nothing in this script can do.",
+      "find": "    report.action = \"squashed\"\n    report.reason = f\"collapsed {report.unpushed} unpushed session commits into one\"",
